{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"a775f02a-9cb1-416b-a320-1db67a21d1ce","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### Investigation \u0026 Root Cause\n\n1. **Producer ([`catalog.build`](file:///workspace/catalog.py#L2-L3))**:\n   - Built catalog keys using [`canonical.key(name)`](file:///workspace/canonical.py#L1-L2), which previously performed `value.strip().lower()`. This stripped whitespace but used standard `.lower()` instead of Unicode casefolding (e.g., characters like `'ß'` were not mapped to `'ss'`).\n   - Stored values were untouched (`{key(name): value for name, value in rows}`).\n\n2. **Consumer ([`query.get`](file:///workspace/query.py#L3-L4))**:\n   - Looked up values directly using `name.lower()` instead of canonicalizing via [`canonical.key(name)`](file:///workspace/canonical.py#L1-L2). It failed to strip whitespace and used `.lower()`.\n\n### Changes Made\n\n- **[`canonical.py`](file:///workspace/canonical.py)**:\n  - Updated [`key(value)`](file:///workspace/canonical.py#L1-L2) to use `value.strip().casefold()`, providing standard Unicode case-insensitive normalization while trimming whitespace.\n- **[`query.py`](file:///workspace/query.py)**:\n  - Updated [`get(catalog, name)`](file:///workspace/query.py#L3-L4) to use `catalog.get(key(name))`, ensuring consumer lookup shares the exact same canonical normalization as producer catalog construction without modifying stored values.\n- **[`tests/test_query.py`](file:///workspace/tests/test_query.py)**:\n  - Added test coverage verifying Unicode casefold equivalences and whitespace stripping across catalog construction and lookup.\n\n### Verification\n\nRan test suite with `python3 -m pytest -q tests`: all 2 test cases passed.\n","duration_seconds":48.711591436,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":195456,"output_tokens":1919,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":56613,"total_tokens":197375}}}
